WEBVTT

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.670
Stop that other truck from coming down.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.020
My Hudson's truck is out of control.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:27.620
Come on.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:35.740
what wound on your head there could stick it hit me in the head otherwise it would hurt

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:46.590
let's see what's wrong with the truck get rid of the hijackers i think i did one what's it

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:50.670
damaged ah broken steering knuckles hold some of that high grade on the other truck

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:56.430
we'll go on into saskatch right oh what's the matter with you are you tired oh

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.330
are you sure that hudson didn't recognize you at the eskimo village oh i'm certain he thinks i was

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:17.930
lost in the shipwreck well you've got to keep out of sight from now on we concentrate on dr miller

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:22.960
and his invention and the doctor must be brought to me alive this must be done in such a way that

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:27.570
no suspicion will be guessed on me you understand yes of course i'll send you out to brandon's place

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.750
there you'll be close to the hudson mine in case you need it

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:33.810
Brock speaking.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.120
All right. Keep in touch.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.800
I knew we shouldn't have stuck our necks out.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.800
Brandon bungled that hijacking job and Hudson got through.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.560
Coming here to see me.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.000
You think it's a bet?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:47.760
Of course not.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.730
I protected myself very carefully.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.260
My importance to our work requires that.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.150
Yes, of course.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:55.800
Yes?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.340
See him in a minute.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.840
Yes, wait in here.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:10.450
All right, send him in.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:15.450
Jim.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:16.090
Hello, Mr. Brock.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:16.730
Good to see you.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:16.930
Thanks.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:17.510
Sit down.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.590
How are things going at the mine?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:20.600
Not so good.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.440
Hijackers again.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.660
But I got that shipment through to your stamp, though.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.950
You know, I can't understand this outbreak of lawlessness.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.670
Though it always seems to be more prevalent in wartimes.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.980
Mr. Brock, I have...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.120
have another truck there's an old one of yours there at the mill i could sure use if you'd sell

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:38.450
it i'd like to accommodate you jim but trucks are hard to get nowadays when will you need it

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:42.240
right away a lot of new machinery came in including the stuff we have to have for the

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.640
sawmill we planned i'd like to get it up to the mine tonight i guess this is the one you mean

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:55.360
isn't it gmq yes that's it you can have it how much i'll take it i'll write your check for it

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.390
right now no hurry why don't you go back by way of the deep close road

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:05.660
road was closed mr rock no the road commissioners have fixed it up i use it quite a lot well it

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:11.750
certainly is a lot closer that way i think i'll use it tonight there you are and i certainly

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:16.450
appreciate that not at all jim very glad to help you any man could make a comeback the way you did

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:21.000
after being wounded in the service deserves all the breaks he can get thanks and if you need any

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.310
help loading your stuff just let me know i'll do that thanks a lot mr brock no doubt

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.890
Thought you were laying off the Hudson outfit.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:34.830
I am.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:36.610
That is, anything violent.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.730
But if Jim Hudson should meet with a fatal accident on his way back to the mine,

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.050
that'd be too bad, wouldn't it?

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:48.320
Yeah, Ruth.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.130
Are you sure I can buy all this equipment in Saskatchewan?

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:51.470
Certainly.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:52.710
You're going to look Jim up anyway.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:53.770
He'll show you where to go.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.190
I mean, if he got there safely.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.350
Nah, he made it all right.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:57.720
Well, I'm on my way, Dad.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:58.940
All right, I'll drive carefully.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:07:59.550
Bye.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:16.970
Don't call it. I forgot something. I forgot to tell you about the first aid kit.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:20.500
It's the only doctor we have here. And the station wagon is our only ambulance.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.740
Do you want me to check it over for you?

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.680
Yes. When you get to town, buy whatever it needs.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.340
Now, is there anything else?

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.620
Well, if there is, I'll probably think of it when you get back.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:29.650
Bye.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:47.560
I don't care how long it takes, we've got to find Pete before somebody else does and identifies him.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.870
Now we'll go back up the road toward the mine.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.420
Spread out a little and keep your eyes peeled.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.220
This man is in a serious condition.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:49.420
You can't move him till I finish dressing his wound.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.300
Act like you know what you're doing.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.580
Thank you. I've done this before.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:57.170
Isn't that car from the gun sight mine?

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:58.640
Is it?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.050
miss miller i might be sure put out a lot of information don't you not my job no then what

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:13.130
is your job right now to care for the wounded fine we've got some more of them bring her along boys

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:17.700
why don't you put the injured man in the station wagon i'll decide what to do put her on a horse

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:22.120
and blindfold her you don't have to force me if they're wounded i'll go willingly noble aren't

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:26.020
you no i'm not noble i'm doing this for a reason you'd never understand

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:35.850
Thank you.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.930
I'll need some alcohol to dress this man's wounds.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.240
That's a good idea.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:06.960
I could use a little snort myself.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:08.790
I want it for sterilizing.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.600
You mean you're going to waste good liquor?

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:11.300
Get it.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:21.400
You're too smart to try to get away from here, aren't you?

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:22.420
Really?

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:25.890
And I thought you were too smart to try to hold me here.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:27.440
We'll see.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:39.960
BR to H.B. BR to H.B.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.400
Young Hudson gave us a slip again, Chief, but I think we...

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.560
From now on, don't try anything till you hear from me.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.660
Sorry, Chief. By the way, we've got Miller's daughter here.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.640
What? Why, all the stupid things.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.320
Couldn't help it. Found Pete and could identify him.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:11:59.980
Well, the only thing to do now is to get...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.420
Get rid of it.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:01.820
Get this set up for the night.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.800
Jim Hudson will be coming up Deep Guts Road.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:09.170
Thank you.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:22.230
men going

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:23.840
to a bridge party.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:24.850
Bridge Party.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:25.500
Yeah.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.720
And your friend Hudson's gonna be dummy.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:29.840
How's he doing?

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:31.500
All fine.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.290
He'll wake up pretty soon and be hungry.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:35.970
I'm hungry right now.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.020
How's about a little food for all of us?

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:38.970
Can you get some?

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.790
Sure, I'll go out to the cook shack and make some sandwiches.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:42.790
Get busy.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.600
When we hit the deep gulch road, we'll stretch out the half-mile intervals.

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:15.670
Okay. Your truck ready to roll?

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:16.620
All set.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:17.450
Let's go.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:37.920
The cable's on this side.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:04.820
It looks good.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:05.910
You know why?

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:07.750
They're a nice-looking girl.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:11.180
And being we're the only ones at camp tonight, we might as well enjoy ourselves.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.370
What were these men doing when they were shot?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.450
prospecting for gold.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:17.700
Jim Hudson?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:19.600
You ain't so dumb.

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:21.120
Neither is Jim Hudson.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.190
He'll wipe you all out before he's through.

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:26.730
Why, after the night, he won't even be able to wipe his own chin?

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.640
Oh, you're referring to that bridge party he's going to have.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:30.970
You catch on quick.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:32.500
Help yourself.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:33.760
May I?

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:34.810
Sure.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.120
I like a gal who can handle her own liquor.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:38.860
You'll be surprised.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:42.010
Well,

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:43.640
It is too.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.000
You name it.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.260
Here's hoping to...

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.240
Thank you.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.660
We'll do the rest.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:37.360
All right.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.040
Rod sold it to him today.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:40.800
Not a bad deal, huh?

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.890
Wilson, is Jim driving that truck up ahead?

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:51.490
Well, yes, but...

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.630
Well, then we've got to catch him.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:16:59.980
Where did you come from?

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:01.380
Is there a bridge near here?

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:03.310
Jim said something about one.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.400
And that's it.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.240
Hurry. We've got to stop it.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.920
I'm going as fast as this truck will go.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:13.640
Thank you.
